cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "serum-ca-cryo: Computational model for post-thaw calcium deficit in cryostored serum QC standards"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2025-04-26"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/tohafrit/serum-ca-cryo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tohafrit/serum-ca-cryo"
abstract: >
  Open-source computational model explaining the mechanism of post-thaw calcium deficit
  in human-serum quality-control standards stored at -20°C for ≥6 months.
  The model quantifies cryoconcentration-driven supersaturation, ACP→OCP→HAp Ostwald
  ripening kinetics at -20°C, stochastic nucleation variability across vials, and
  three intervention protocols (degassing, controlled-rate freezing, vortex thaw).
  All figures and data tables are fully reproducible via `make all`.
